Prompt: draft_scene.j2
Service Step: DRAFT_SCENE (Advanced Scene-Level Writing Mode: Body Text)
Function Description: Write a single scene body according to the current scene contract, only fulfilling the scene's exclusive events/revelations/state changes.
Upstream Input: stage_cards, current_scene, completed_scene_handoffs, adjacent_scene_handoffs,
         chapter_number, target_word_count, reading_power_hint
Downstream Output: TEXT: Current scene body text, without title, scene_id, Markdown, or explanatory notes.
Downstream Consumers: draft._draft_scene_level_text, scene_writing.stitch_scene_texts,
         subsequent editing/quality checking/fixing and persistence workflows
Consumption Chain Priority: P0 = Write only the current scene without leaking other scenes' owned facts;
         P1 = Catch dependency scene handoffs and deliver this scene's handoff_to_next;
         P2 = Style, voice, sensory details, and expression quality
================================================================================
#}
